Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?dos:=20Phase=2011=20patch=200052=20=E2=80=94=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?fix=20CloseDevice=2016-bit=20DSP=20teardown=20(wub-after-quit)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

iter N+1 (2026-05-11) operator on g2k SB16 PnP CTL0026 / DSP v4.13 reported
persistent "wub-wub-wub" DSP residual after quit-to-DOS on all 3 PLAY cells.
flush-instr root-cause analysis in docs/PHASE11-WAVE-28-FINDINGS-N-PLUS-1.md
§ 4: SDL3 DOS audio CloseDevice's 16-bit teardown branch emits the wrong
commands; SB16 16-bit DMA channel keeps replaying the last 256-frame ring
chunk in auto-init mode after process exit (~23 ms period @ 11025 Hz =
audible "wub" loop).

Root cause: latent command mismatch in the 16-bit branch, predates the
Phase-10/11 patch series (origin in PR-#15377 import):

  if (hidden->is_16bit) {
      WriteSoundBlasterDSP(0xDA);  // comment says "exit 16-bit auto-init"
      WriteSoundBlasterDSP(0xD3);  // turn off speaker
  }

But per the patch 0038 SDP-command documentation at line ~410, 0xDA is
"exit 8-bit auto-init DMA" — a no-op on the 16-bit DMA channel. 0xD3
only disables the analog output stage; DMA fetching continues. The
16-bit DAC halt command (0xD5) and 16-bit auto-init exit command (0xD9)
were never issued from CloseDevice.

DSP command semantics (SB16 spec, cross-confirmed against patch 0038's
inline doc):
  0xD0 = halt 8-bit DAC          (pre-SB16)
  0xD3 = turn off speaker (line-level only)
  0xD5 = halt 16-bit DAC          (SB16-class)
  0xD9 = exit 16-bit auto-init DMA mode
  0xDA = exit 8-bit auto-init DMA mode

Fix: emit 0xD5 + 0xD9 + 0xD3 in the 16-bit branch — halt-DAC,
exit-auto-init, speaker-off. Mirrors the working 8-bit branch's
0xD0 + 0xDA + 0xD3 pattern.

Distinct from iter L freeze-on-quit (SDL/0050 cooperative-scheduler-vs-
MIX_DestroyMixer deadlock per sdl_0050_ship_with_freeze.md). That path
never reaches CloseDevice; user accepted the freeze trade. This patch
addresses the orthogonal "we returned to DOS but DMA leaked" case.
SDL/0050's behavior is unchanged — quiescence gate logic in GetDeviceBuf
runs on the audio thread before any CloseDevice work; the two paths
don't interact.

8-bit branch left untouched (its 0xD0/0xDA/0xD3 sequence is correct as-is
for the 8-bit DMA channel; only triggered on FORCE_SB_8BIT or DSP < 4).

DOSBox-X smoke insufficient validation per dosbox_not_behavioral_proxy_for_io.md
— real-HW operator iter required for confirmation. Patch rides along
with wave-29's next iter per maximum_payload_per_iter.md; no dedicated
CF-swap window.

One TU touched (src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c). ~32 lines added (mostly
the inline reasoning comment + one doskutsu_dbg_log marker); 3 lines of
actual logic change (1 command swap + 2 new commands inserted).
---
 src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c | 34 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 33 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c b/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
index 296c43253..e39bba163 100644
--- a/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
+++ b/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
@@ -1036,7 +1036,39 @@ static void DOSSOUNDBLASTER_CloseDevice(SDL_AudioDevice *device)
             // Disable PCM (normal path; force-pause branch already hard-
             // reset the DSP and skips this).
             if (hidden->is_16bit) {
-                WriteSoundBlasterDSP(0xDA); // exit 16-bit auto-init DMA
+                /* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 11 patch 0052): fix 16-bit teardown
+                   command mismatch — root cause of iter N+1 wub-after-quit
+                   on SB16 PnP CTL0026 (g2k). Pre-patch this branch emitted
+                   0xDA + 0xD3 — but 0xDA is "exit 8-bit auto-init DMA"
+                   (per the patch 0038 comment at line ~410), a no-op on
+                   the 16-bit DMA channel. The 16-bit halt + exit-auto-init
+                   commands were never issued; 0xD3 only disables the
+                   analog output stage, not DMA fetching. SB16 16-bit DAC
+                   kept replaying the last 256-frame ring chunk in auto-
+                   init mode after process exit — audible "wub-wub-wub"
+                   loop at ~23 ms period (256 frames @ 11025 Hz).
+
+                   Correct sequence mirrors the working 8-bit branch
+                   (halt-DAC then exit-auto-init then speaker-off):
+                     0xD5 = halt 16-bit DAC          (SB16-class)
+                     0xD9 = exit 16-bit auto-init DMA
+                     0xD3 = turn off speaker
+
+                   Latent bug; predates the Phase-10/11 patch series
+                   (origin in PR-#15377 import). Per `sdl_ai_policy.md`
+                   stays workspace-local. Per
+                   `sdl_0050_ship_with_freeze.md` this is orthogonal to
+                   the SDL/0050 cooperative-scheduler-vs-MIX_DestroyMixer
+                   freeze trade — that path doesn't reach CloseDevice; the
+                   wub-after-quit case is "we returned to DOS but DMA
+                   leaked." Real-HW iter N+1 (2026-05-11) is the surfacing
+                   trace; flush-instr's
+                   docs/PHASE11-WAVE-28-FINDINGS-N-PLUS-1.md § 4 is the
+                   root-cause analysis. */
+                doskutsu_dbg_log("audio close: 16-bit DSP halt-then-exit "
+                                 "(0xD5/0xD9/0xD3)");
+                WriteSoundBlasterDSP(0xD5); // halt 16-bit DAC
+                WriteSoundBlasterDSP(0xD9); // exit 16-bit auto-init DMA
                 WriteSoundBlasterDSP(0xD3); // turn off the speaker
             } else {
                 WriteSoundBlasterDSP(0xD0); // halt 8-bit DMA
